:" A 16-tap FIR filter over a block of 256 samples, giving 241 outputs.

   A reference program of the static profile (docs/static-profile.md). The
   tables are built on the host, when the program is compiled: raw is used
   only to compute taps and is not part of the compiled program; taps (16
   floats that sum to 1) and idx (a 16 by 241 table of sample positions)
   become constant data.

   Check it:   kgpy check examples/embedded/fir.kg
   Expected:   examples/embedded/fir.expect
"

raw::{1.0+x&15-x}'!16
taps::raw%+/raw
idx::+{x+!16}'!241

run::{+/taps*x@idx}

.entry("run";"float[256] -> float[241]")
